  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe report door (PR #1798) copies a picture of the application window to the clipboard. If the read-back map fails (a lost device), the capture callback drops the waiting tokens and leaves `in_flight` false. The timeout in `due()` then cannot fire. The status text stays at \"copying the whole window\".\n\nThe failure is rare. The text report still works.\n\n## Source\n\nFinding 2 of the review of PR #1798 at head `40d967840026f5cf2193d2d68537efcc4895bcae` (comment 7004545700). The review found this by a reading of the code. No test shows it.\n\n## What should happen\n\n- When the read-back fails, the status line says that the picture was not copied and that the text report is complete.\n- A test pins the status text after a failed read-back.\n\nRefs #1696\n",
